  "query_preview": "..\nUpper-level ridging will build over the region today through \nFriday leading to high temperatures 15-20 degrees above average \nfor this time of the year. By Friday the ridge starts to track \neastward allowing the upper-level low currently positioned over \nthe western CONUS to advance further east. Southerly flow aloft \nover the weekend will push moisture into Southwest Montana \nallowing for a chance of light rain along the lower elevations and\nlight snow above 7000ft. The advancement of the trough through \nthe weekend will allow for temperatures to gradually decrease \ntowards seasonal averages by early next week.\n\nThrough the middle of next week, a more unsettled pattern is \nexpected to set up with multiple low pressure systems expected to \nmove through bringing multiple chances for mountain snow and lower \nelevation rain/snow. A high degree of uncertainty remains in exactly \nhow these systems will play out, especially towards the end of next \nweek. But the overall trend points towards a cooler and wetter \npattern lasting through next weekend. -thor",
